# What the PyPI packages need in CI beyond Python itself, pinned, in a file a
# bot can edit.
#
# python/testing-files-generator is tested with pytest in ci.yml, and
# .github/workflows/pypi.yml installs the wheels of a release with uv as well
# as pip, because uv keeps a binary's execute bit only when the wheel says it
# was made on Unix and pip keeps it either way (docs/PYTEST-2026-11-09.md).
# tomli reads pyproject.toml for release/assemble.py on Python 3.10, which has
# no tomllib - it is the library tomllib was taken from. None of them is
# linked into either binary or shipped in a wheel, and go.mod never sees them.
#
# The metadata of the wheels is checked by pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish, which
# runs twine check before it uploads anything. twine is not here because its
# own tree did not install on Python 3.10 and brought a licence the dependency
# gate cannot read (docs/REVIEW-226-2026-11-09.md).
#
# Licences read from the pinned versions rather than recalled, on 2026-11-09,
# from the metadata on PyPI: pytest MIT, uv MIT OR Apache-2.0, tomli MIT (and
# the LICENSE file of its tag 2.5.0).
#
# requirements-pypi.txt next to this file is compiled from it by pip-compile,
# the same way requirements-semgrep.txt is, so Dependabot proposes a set pip
# can install. It is compiled on Python 3.10, the oldest the package declares,
# because a set resolved on a newer Python can pin a version 3.10 cannot
# install. To compile it by hand, from the root of the repository:
#
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/.github:/w" -w /w python:3.10-slim sh -c "pip install -q pip==26.1.1 pip-tools==7.5.3 && pip-compile --strip-extras --no-emit-index-url --output-file=requirements-pypi.txt requirements-pypi.in"
pytest==9.2.0
tomli==2.5.0 ; python_version < "3.11"
uv==0.13.7
